    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39181" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prō-tūbĕro</span></b> ,
			āre, v. n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to swell</i> or <i>bulge out</i>, <i>to grow forth</i> (late Lat.),
					<i><span class="en">Sol. 45</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">poma,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 46 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">densa ne supra modum protuberent,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Idyll. 13</span></i>
			, praef. § 8; cf. <i><span class="en">id. ib. 16,
				10</span></i>.</div>
